From 1b442642e153dcdfc08f1e5cec2171893efef826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:32:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Copy names and other text into fixed buffers as text, not as
 formats

Thirteen sites passed text from the server, the user or a file to sprintf,
_snprintf_s or fprintf as the format. A % in a pet, homunculus, couple,
char-server or character name, or in a typed name, made the client read
arguments that were never passed; %n stops it. Packet fields were also
read up to the next NUL, past a full field.

Each site now copies the text with "%s", or "%.*s" bounded by the packet
field, through _snprintf_s(..., _TRUNCATE, ...) bounded by the buffer:

- homun_name (companion_packets.c), from ZC_PROPERTY_HOMUN: both service
  type paths are merged into one bounded copy of the 24-byte name.
- pet_named (actor_names.c), from ZC_ACK_REQNAME and ZC_ACK_REQNAMEALL:
  NAME_LENGTH bytes into petName[32].
- game_mode_zc_property_pet (packets_pet.c): the 24-byte name field.
- game_mode_zc_couple_name (packets_social.c): the 24-byte name into
  couple_name[24]; a full field is cut to 23 bytes instead of writing a
  25th byte into name_balloon.
- game_mode_update_cut_in (packets_world.c): the cut-in image name into
  g_illustImageName[0x100].
- server_list (login_states.c): the 20-byte char-server name after the
  optional "new" prefix, into the rest of text[0x40].
- game_mode_move_to_server (mode_connection.c): the map name, into the
  20 bytes of mapName and map_name_tail as before.
- ui_homun_info_wnd_on_create and homun_rename (companion_info.c): the
  job name used as the default name and the name the user typed, into
  homunName[0x20].
- ui_pet_info_wnd_on_create and pet_rename (pet_info.c): the same two
  copies into petName[32].
- ui_my_style_wnd_save_slots (styling_shop.c): the saved records, which
  hold character names, are written with fputs instead of fprintf.
- change_began state 0x27c (state_messages_timed.c): the line formatted
  from msg 0x784 was formatted a second time, so a % in its output (as
  from %%) read a missing argument; it is now copied into the 0x100-byte
  line.

Validation: the new test_name_text runs the extracted production code:
homun_name, pet_named, game_mode_zc_property_pet,
game_mode_zc_couple_name, game_mode_update_cut_in and server_list whole,
and from the larger functions the statement that fills the buffer. Every
text holds "a%d%x%%b" or "%s%n%s%n" and must arrive unchanged; full packet
fields followed by other bytes, a 319-byte image name, a 26-character map
name and 36-character typed names must be cut to the field or buffer;
couple_name must not touch name_balloon. 41 cases. With any one of the
eleven files reverted the test fails. Release build without warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
